Van semi‑trailers are enclosed‑cargo box trailers used for transporting general goods. They typically consist of a metal or composite cargo box, a supporting frame and hinged doors that protect cargo from rain, dust and other environmental factors. These units are among the most widely deployed vehicle types in logistics, serving e‑commerce delivery, express freight and industrial goods transport.
