What is a Van Semi-trailer?
A van semi‑trailer is a body‑type attachment mounted on a tractor unit, providing a sealed compartment for cargo. Unlike rigid trucks, the semi‑trailer separates the driving cab from the cargo space, allowing greater flexibility in fleet composition and easier load distribution. The design focuses on weather‑proofing, structural integrity, and ease of loading/unloading through standardized doors and lock mechanisms. Manufacturers continuously refine the chassis, door systems, and material composition to meet evolving regulatory, efficiency, and safety requirements.
